A1. This is always hanging around a picture at the Metropolitan. ~ FRAME
A5. Anthropologists and women are forever harping about this. ~ MAN
A7. What does the ambitious Solomon Islander try to get? ~ AHEAD
A11. Name something besides applesauce that apples are found in. ~ CRATE
A13. This gives down occasionally. ~ EIDER
A15. "Going on the water wagon" would do this to a flapper's reputation. ~ MAR
A17. Things that are "all wet" are apt to be this way. ~ SODDEN
A19. A Danish Island in the Baltic Sea. ~ AERO
A21. What does it mean to "choose"? ~ ELECT
A23. This is what a pedestrian should be as well as a "good looker." ~ DODGER
A25. A well known news service (init.). ~ AP
A26. What King Alphonso's "yes-men" say. ~ SI
A27. There is nothing counterfeit about this kind of thing. ~ REAL
A28. What burden did the Boys in Gray have to bear? ~ LETTERS
A30. This is one way of doing a good turn. ~ VEER
A32. A snake got this little girl in trouble. ~ EVE
A33. A pronoun. ~ ME
A34. What a wife does rather than ask. ~ DEMANDS
A36. Entertainers of note. ~ SINGERS
A40. This indicates satisfaction. ~ OK
A41. What is often between this and that? ~ OR
A42. What should all detectives and dope fiends have? ~ WATSONS
A46. What is the first thing the bull fighter does to the bull? ~ ENRAGES
A49. Who first surveys a new territory? (Init.) ~ CE
A50. The proper way to address a United States battleship. ~ USS
A51. These get drunk in England. ~ ALES
A52. An English philosopher also famous as a mathematician. ~ RUSSELL
A55. A good bond holder. ~ SAFE
A56. The proper address of an ordinary steamship. ~ SS
A58. A preposition of place. ~ AT
A59. To do this makes one hateful. ~ LOATHE
A61. What would a person be who had an old head on young shoulders? ~ FECAK
A63. This word adds emphasis. ~ VERY
A65. This is the way of all flesh. ~ CARNAL
A67. A naval affirmative. ~ AYE
A68. What kind of people arouse the State Department's moral sense? ~ ALIEN
A70. What days bring the most sunshine into the lives of men? ~ CLEAR
A72. Name something you could never get on a chorus girl. ~ STAYS
A73. One way to get action. ~ SUE
A74. Famous for its black eye. ~ SUSAN

D1. Where there's a fire you'll find these. ~ FUMES
D2. What is 43,560 sq. feet of earth? ~ ACRE
D3. What do we say before calling a man a name? ~ MR
D4. What kind of people did Horace Greeley advise to go West? ~ EASTERN
D5. What does a reformer do for a living? ~ MEDDLES
D6. These stir up action—after you get the point. ~ NEEDLES
D7. Name some one thing on page 27 of Judge. ~ AD
D8. What kind of trouble does a lot of loving usually cause? ~ HEART
D9. This means "before " to poets. ~ ERE
D10. Aviators should never take these for their health. ~ DROPS
D12. What is the sign of the infinitive? ~ TO
D14. An English dean. ~ INGE
D16. As long as man kicks you will know he is this. ~ ALIVE
D18. To accomplish. ~ DO
D20. What are corset salesmen getting nowadays? ~ RARER
D22. What are heard on the back stairs of haunted houses? ~ CREAKS
D24. Name a place where they teach the best English. ~ ETON
D29. What do societ" girls do at a "coming out party?" ~ EMERGE
D31. What does a movie gal do when she sees a camera? ~ EMOTES
D34. No "keep off the grass" sign effects this. ~ DEW
D35. A racket. ~ DIN
D37. An electrocuted atom. ~ ION
D38. A goal maker. (If you are not particular about your grammar.) ~ GOALEE
D39. Who was that lady your wife seen you with—if you're lucky? ~ SIS
D43. Sharp; penetrating. ~ ACUTE
D44. A substitute for the goat's butter. ~ OLEO
D45. These are known by the women they keep. ~ SULTANS
D46. No perfume would be worth a scent without this. ~ ESSENCE
D47. Lotteries. ~ RAFFLES
D48. An expository literary form popularized by Montaigne. ~ ESSAY
D52. What a raving maniac does for amusement. ~ RAVES
D53. An adverb denoting foxy ways. ~ SLYLY
D54. This is very much attached to feminine undie-apparel. ~ LACE
D57. The yarn grandma spun. ~ SKEIN
D60. What working men work by (abbr.). ~ HR
D62. Listening-in devices. ~ CARS
D64. What would abbreviate Royal Artillery Accidents? ~ RAA
D66. Who would any crossword puzzle maker nominate for president? ~ AL
D69. The third person sing. present indicative of "be." ~ IS
D71. This means "to the" in French. ~ AU


Misprints, kept as printed (printed → meant):
D29: What do societ" girls do at a "coming out party?" → society

